00:50:39.040 --> 00:50:43.210
I would rather say that there are ways
of figuring out how valuable you are,

00:50:43.210 --> 00:50:45.650
that are independent of
those traditional signals.

00:50:45.650 --> 00:50:46.510
Whether you have them or not.

00:50:48.230 --> 00:50:49.920
So I would say today I've changed my mind.

00:50:49.920 --> 00:50:54.040
But by the way, that's another thing.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:55.636
&gt;&gt; Changing your mind.

00:50:55.636 --> 00:50:57.744
&gt;&gt; Is so powerful.

00:50:57.744 --> 00:50:59.320
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:50:59.320 --> 00:51:01.150
&gt;&gt; I mean, fuck, change your mind.

00:51:01.150 --> 00:51:04.410
It makes for really,
really, really, bursty,

00:51:04.410 --> 00:51:06.550
difficult marriages at times.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:51:06.550 --> 00:51:09.350
&gt;&gt; My wife will tell you.

00:51:09.350 --> 00:51:12.230
But man, is it powerful in business.

00:51:12.230 --> 00:51:14.350
Change your mind all the time.

00:51:15.510 --> 00:51:16.360
And it's amazing,

00:51:16.360 --> 00:51:21.430
again, where you'll find really good
scaled leaders want the right answer.

00:51:21.430 --> 00:51:24.500
And they're fine with capitulation,
they're fine with change.

00:51:24.500 --> 00:51:26.980
They really are,
because they just want the right answer.

00:51:26.980 --> 00:51:29.880
And then you just get so
invested in an answer.

00:51:29.880 --> 00:51:34.020
And then you build up all this
superficial logic to reinforce it,

00:51:34.020 --> 00:51:38.030
versus saying I don't know,
you know what, I changed my mind.

00:51:38.030 --> 00:51:39.980
Wow, another powerful thing I think.

00:51:41.130 --> 00:51:44.990
I change my mind all the time.
&gt;&gt; I think this is going to be our last

00:51:44.990 --> 00:51:48.120
