00:52:05.591 --> 00:52:07.093
I don't know, fucking buy some bonds?

00:52:07.093 --> 00:52:08.872
I mean, I don't know.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:52:08.872 --> 00:52:10.901
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:52:10.901 --> 00:52:11.846
&gt;&gt; Here's what I would tell

00:52:11.846 --> 00:52:12.357
you, man.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:52:12.357 --> 00:52:13.526
&gt;&gt; I think,

00:52:13.526 --> 00:52:17.790
if you ask me,
who's building the most important,

00:52:17.790 --> 00:52:20.240
indelible company in the world,
I've been very public about this.

00:52:20.240 --> 00:52:21.850
I think it's Jeff Bezos.

00:52:21.850 --> 00:52:25.130
Part of what he realized was
the value of slow-compounding.

00:52:25.130 --> 00:52:28.820
So here's my little theory
about company value creation.

00:52:28.820 --> 00:52:31.730
The faster you build it,
that is the half-life,

00:52:31.730 --> 00:52:34.000
it will get destroyed in
the same amount of time.

00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:38.660
And so when you think about a lot of
social businesses, that's played out.

00:52:38.660 --> 00:52:43.290
And when you see what sort
of the tops are like,

00:52:43.290 --> 00:52:47.530
does it take, eight, nine, ten years to
build a really great consumer business?

00:52:47.530 --> 00:52:51.070
It'll take 8, 9, 10,
12 years to destroy it.

00:52:51.070 --> 00:52:54.370
And we may see the tipping point now
in a couple of these businesses.

00:52:54.370 --> 00:52:57.210
Right now we may be seeing it in front
of our eyes, regulatory or otherwise.

00:52:57.210 --> 00:52:58.839
So why is that an important statement?

00:53:01.400 --> 00:53:04.625
Amassing capital to me,
is about finding a smart,

00:53:04.625 --> 00:53:08.610
useful solution to a very hard,
practical problem.

00:53:08.610 --> 00:53:09.990
And being slow and methodical.

00:53:11.080 --> 00:53:14.790
And again, that's what I'm saying,
you have to rewire your brain for

00:53:14.790 --> 00:53:15.820
that to be okay.

00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:22.280
How do you, in year two or year five,
[COUGH] come back to this room for

00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:25.565
your, what is it called when you get-
&gt;&gt; Reunion.

00:53:25.565 --> 00:53:27.496
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:53:27.496 --> 00:53:30.210
&gt;&gt; [COUGH] And say I'm still

00:53:30.210 --> 00:53:33.950
working on the same thing, and
when somebody says, and how is it going?

00:53:33.950 --> 00:53:37.555
You have the courage to say, it's hard, I
haven't figured it out yet, I don't know.

00:53:39.670 --> 00:53:45.230
But if you figure it out and you have this
moderate growth, moderate compounding,

00:53:45.230 --> 00:53:49.290
that is the key, that's cool.

00:53:49.290 --> 00:53:54.290
I look at our returns and it's so
funny, because you can get so

00:53:54.290 --> 00:53:56.770
enthralled by IRRs in our business.

00:53:58.000 --> 00:54:02.250
And I have friends who run
other organizations, and

00:54:02.250 --> 00:54:06.693
they're like, we posted 92% IRR,
and I'm like,

00:54:06.693 --> 00:54:09.320
well you can't eat IRR.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:54:09.320 --> 00:54:12.360
&gt;&gt; What does it really mean?

00:54:12.360 --> 00:54:17.190
And when you unpack it, what you realize
is, fast money returns can completely,

00:54:17.190 --> 00:54:19.575
really decay long-term thinking and
sound judgment.

00:54:20.630 --> 00:54:25.507
And so I'm like wow, I would really
love to just compound at 15% a year.

00:54:25.507 --> 00:54:26.407
And the reason is,

00:54:26.407 --> 00:54:30.300
because if I can do that for 50 years,
that's 250 fucking billion dollars.

00:54:30.300 --> 00:54:34.567
It's some crazy number,
it's just enormous, so it's slow and

00:54:34.567 --> 00:54:36.750
steady against heart problems.

00:54:37.850 --> 00:54:40.650
Start by turning off your social apps and
giving your brain a break.

00:54:42.140 --> 00:54:44.739
because then you will at least
be a little bit more motivated,

00:54:44.739 --> 00:54:47.680
to not be motivated by everybody
else fucking thinks about you.

00:54:47.680 --> 00:54:48.950
Do you know what I'm saying?

00:54:48.950 --> 00:54:50.780
It's hard, think about how all
this stuff plays together.

00:54:50.780 --> 00:54:55.285
How does trying to get,
posting your fucking waffles online,

00:54:55.285 --> 00:54:57.835
relate to me starting a business and

00:54:57.835 --> 00:55:00.130
accumulating capital.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:55:00.130 --> 00:55:01.920
&gt;&gt; This is wiring your brain for

00:55:01.920 --> 00:55:03.140
super fast feedback.

00:55:03.140 --> 00:55:05.800
It's the same brain you're
using to build a company.

00:55:05.800 --> 00:55:08.462
Don't think they're not the same.
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:55:08.462 --> 00:55:09.330
&gt;&gt; Do you know what I'm saying?

00:55:10.750 --> 00:55:11.520
No, yes?

00:55:11.520 --> 00:55:12.265
No?
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:55:12.265 --> 00:55:13.840
&gt;&gt; Yes, yes, right?

00:55:14.980 --> 00:55:15.570
You have one brain!

00:55:17.730 --> 00:55:19.951
So you're training your brain here,
whether you think it or not,

00:55:19.951 --> 00:55:22.063
whether you know it or not,
whether you acknowledge it or not.

00:55:22.063 --> 00:55:26.745
Acknowledge that these things,
where you're spending hours a day,

00:55:26.745 --> 00:55:29.930
are rewiring your psychology and
physiology.

00:55:29.930 --> 00:55:31.943
In a way,
that now you have to use to go and

00:55:31.943 --> 00:55:34.800
figure out how to be productive
in the commercial world.

00:55:35.830 --> 00:55:37.250
So if you don't change this,

00:55:37.250 --> 00:55:39.260
you are going to get the same
behavior as over here.

00:55:41.210 --> 00:55:45.840
Change this, there's a reason why
Steve Jobs was anti social media.

00:55:47.002 --> 00:55:47.740
I am telling you,

00:55:47.740 --> 00:55:52.390
I'm not on these fucking apps, I'm not
him by any stretch of the imagination.

00:55:52.390 --> 00:55:57.018
But I am proactively trying to rewire
my brain chemistry to not be short

00:55:57.018 --> 00:55:58.045
term focused.

00:55:59.721 --> 00:56:02.619
I'm telling you they're linked.
&gt;&gt; Kumar,

00:56:02.619 --> 00:56:05.854
thank you so much for being here and
enlightening all of us.

00:56:05.854 --> 00:56:15.331
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

